// Practice quiz: Python review
// Formative, low-stakes retention practice. First draft, not reviewed. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: python/fastapi-services/python-review

::o1 is vs equals::a \= [1]; b \= a; c \= [1]. Which is true? {
=a is b is True and a is c is False #Correct. b names the same object, while c is equal but separate.
~a is c is True #Not quite. Two separate lists are not the same object, even when equal.
~a \=\= c is False #Not quite. Their contents are equal.
~a is b is False #Not quite. b is another name for the same list.
}

::o1 comprehension filter::What is [x * 2 for x in [1, 2, 3] if x !\= 2]? {
=[2, 6] #Correct. The filter skips 2, and the rest double.
~[2, 4, 6] #Not quite. The filter removes the value 2.
~[1, 3] #Not quite. The kept values are doubled.
~[4] #Not quite. That keeps only the value the filter removes.
}

::o1 finally::A try block returns a value and a finally block prints a message. Does the message print? {
=Yes, finally runs before the function returns #Correct. finally runs on the way out, whether by return or by exception.
~No, return skips finally #Not quite. finally still runs.
~Only if an exception happened #Not quite. It runs either way.
~Only when the return value is None #Not quite. The value makes no difference.
}

::o2 stage validation::Rows with a non-numeric qty load into staging and later break a results route. Where is the best first fix? {
=Validate before loading, and record rejected rows #Correct. Stop bad rows at the stage responsible, and keep them for review.
~Hide the error in the route #Not quite. That leaves bad data in place.
~Delete the route #Not quite. That removes the feature, not the cause.
~Increase the httpx timeout #Not quite. No outbound call is involved.
}

::o2 stage timeout::Requests to your API hang whenever the Spring Boot service stalls. Which stage holds the defect? {
=The outbound call, which has no bounded timeout #Correct. A deliberate timeout turns a stall into a clear response.
~The Pydantic request model #Not quite. Validation runs before the call and is not waiting on it.
~The CSV generator #Not quite. Extract is not part of this request path.
~The upsert #Not quite. Loading is not part of this request path.
}

::o2 stage aliasing::Every loaded row ends up with the same growing tags list. What is the likely cause? {
=One list object was reused for every record #Correct. Each record shares the object, so an append shows up on them all.
~A missing response model #Not quite. That affects output fields, not how tags accumulate.
~A missing timeout #Not quite. That affects outbound calls.
~ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING #Not quite. That would keep old rows, not grow one list.
}
